license: MIT
keywords:
  - geotechnical engineering
  - bearing capacity
  - sensitivity analysis
  - monte carlo
  - morris screening
  - decision support
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  A sandbox in which a site (DEM, boreholes, climate, vegetation) is discretised
  into blocks, each holding a replaceable layered column, and in which an
  engineering or management intervention is applied and scored against explicit
  feasibility criteria (bearing capacity, settlement, slope stability, lander
  footpad capacity, ecological sustainability). The point is not to predict one
  site but to answer whether replacing a component flips the verdict, and how
  stable that answer is under uncertain inputs. Deterministic solvers are
  replaceable through a registry, and uncertainty is reported as a probability
  of failure (Monte Carlo) and a screening ranking (Morris), not as a single
  factor of safety.
